#
# ============================================================================
# Trading flash cards — hourly push notifications, broad curriculum
# ============================================================================
# Bite-sized education that fires every hour 8 AM - 8 PM ET on weekdays.
# Cards rotate through nine topic pools — each hour maps to ONE topic,
# the specific card within a topic cycles by day-of-year. See the
# HOURLY_TOPIC dict in backend/flashcards/flashcards.py for the full
# hour-to-topic schedule.
#
# Topics covered (9 pools, ~80 cards total):
#   * entry / risk / sell_rules / psychology / review (Minervini)
#   * fundamentals — EPS, P/E vs PEG, FCF, ROIC, book value, equity types
#                    (added 2026-05-21: user asked about "company equity
#                    vs shareholder equity" gap)
#   * market_structure — T+1, dark pools, LULD bands, NBBO, Greeks, halts
#   * history — Livermore, LTCM, Archegos, GME squeeze, flash crash, etc.
#                (the "fun facts traders get stoked by" pool)
#   * edge_math — expectancy, Kelly, drawdown math, compounding, R-multiples
#
# Single cron entry — the script itself decides whether to fire based on
# the current hour (no-op outside the populated window). Beats 13
# separate cron lines and the schedule lives in one place (the Python).
#
# User can mute via /notifications → "Minervini flash cards" toggle.
# Default ON for new subscriptions. NOTE: pref key kept as
# "minervini_flashcards" for backward compat with existing subscriptions —
# the label in the UI may be renamed but the key shouldn't move.
#
# Manual ad-hoc fires for testing:
#   docker compose exec cron python -m flashcards.flashcards hourly
#   docker compose exec cron python -m flashcards.flashcards history     # any topic
#   docker compose exec cron python -m flashcards.flashcards fundamentals
#
# Every hour, EVERY day (weekends too — education isn't time-zone-locked).
# The HOURLY_TOPIC map in flashcards.py covers 0-23 so every fire has a
# valid topic. Quiet-hours pref (per-user, default 22:00-08:00 if enabled)
# suppresses delivery during the user's chosen sleep window — see
# push/subs.py _is_in_quiet_hours.
0      *     *    *    *    /usr/local/bin/python -m flashcards.flashcards hourly
